From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bazel: the Python bindings build from an external repository
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenRoad-py.i imports src/odb/src/swig/common/odb.i and
src/utl/src/Logger-py.i by their path from the repository root. That
resolves from the execroot when OpenROAD is the main repository, and
nowhere when it is an external one (external/openroad+/src/...), so
@openroad//:openroad_py failed in swig:

  Error: Unable to find 'src/odb/src/swig/common/odb.i'

The repository root is now one of openroad_swig-py's swig includes.

Not upstreamed. Retires on the //:bump onto an OpenROAD whose
@openroad//:openroad_py builds as a dependency.
---
diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index ac30a5ea..e51f604e 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -417,6 +417,10 @@ python_wrap_cc(
     module = "ord_py",
     root_swig_src = "src/OpenRoad-py.i",
     swig_includes = [
+        # OpenRoad-py.i imports src/odb/... and src/utl/... from the
+        # repository root, which is not the execroot when OpenROAD is an
+        # external repository.
+        ".",
         "include",
         "src",
     ],
